>> title: Burrito Bowl
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: chicken, rice, black beans, mexican, skillet, bowl
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: burrito bowl, chipotle bowl, mission bowl, taco bowl, rice bowl, grain bowl, burrito without the tortilla
>> pairs-with: taco-seasoning, guacamole, salsa-verde-cruda, crema-mexicana
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr
>> step.1: The lime goes in after the rice is cooked and never with it. Acid in the pot keeps the grain from softening.
>> step.2: simmer 18 min, rest 10 min, lime last
>> step.3: rub, then marinate 30 min
>> step.4: sear 10 min, rest 5 min, chop
>> step.5: simmer 10 min, until it coats
>> step.6: build it, beans beside the rice

The lime goes in after the rice is cooked, never with it. Acid in the pot keeps the grain from softening, and what you get is chalky rice that smells right.

Simmer @long-grain white rice{1 1/2%cups}(300 g; rinsed) in @water{2 1/4%cups}(530 mL) with @kosher salt{1%tsp} covered ~simmer{18%min}, then ~rest{10%min} off the heat and fork through @lime{1}(juiced) and @cilantro{1/3%cup}(chopped).

Rub @chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; boneless) with @taco seasoning{2%Tbs} and @chipotles in adobo{2}(minced), then ~marinate{30%min}.

Sear @&(~1)chicken{} in a hot #cast iron skillet{} ~sear{10%min}, turning once, until the spice crust is dark and dry, then ~rest{5%min} and chop into rough cubes.

Simmer @black beans{15%oz}(425 g; canned, with their liquid) with @ground cumin{1%tsp} and @garlic{2%cloves}(sliced) ~simmer{10%min}, until the liquid goes glossy and coats the beans rather than covering them.

Spoon @&(~4)lime rice{} into four bowls, add @&(~1)black beans{} and @&(~2)chopped chicken{}, and finish with @romaine{2%cups}(shredded), @cotija{2%oz}(60 g; crumbled), @pickled jalapeños{2%Tbs} and @lime{1}(in wedges).
